nd-layer2 @sm:h-[51px] @sm:w-[50px] ml-[-10px]\"><img alt=\"en_alexander\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"size-full object-cover\" style=\"color:transparent\" src=\"https://cdn.ainvest.com/articles/focusnews/coverimage/content/pictures/alexander_9990f0971755765042310.png?format=webp\"></span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"flex min-w-0 items-center ml-[2px]\">\n         <div class=\"flex min-w-0 flex-wrap items-center text-[14px] font-semibold leading-[18px] text-text-primary @sm:text-[16px] @sm:leading-[22px]\">\n          <span class=\"mr-[6px]\">AI Podcast:</span><span>Your News, Now Playing</span>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n       <button aria-label=\"Play podcast\" class=\"flex min-h-[32px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-[6px] rounded-full px-[12px] py-[6px] @sm:min-h-[42px] @sm:px-[20px] @sm:py-[10px] cursor-not-allowed bg-button-brand-disabled text-button-brand-text-default\" disabled title=\"loading...\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"text-nowrap text-[14px] font-[590] leading-[14px] text-button-brand-text-default\">Loading</span></button>\n      </div>\n     </section>\n     <section class=\"NewsDetailAimeSummary-module__CfDn9a__summaryContainer relative mb-[24px] flex w-full flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-[16px] border px-[16px] backdrop-blur-[15px] @sm:px-[20px]\">\n      <button aria-expanded=\"true\" aria-label=\"Collapse Aime summary\" class=\"flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-[16px] py-[12px] text-left @sm:py-[16px]\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"flex min-w-0 items-center gap-[16px]\"><span class=\"truncate text-[16px] font-bold leading-[22px] text-text-primary @sm:text-[18px] @sm:leading-[26px]\">Aime Summary</span></span></button>\n      <div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-[16px] pb-[16px] @sm:pb-[24px]\">\n       <div aria-labelledby=\"news-detail-aime-summary-tab-overview\" class=\"flex w-full items-stretch min-h-[100px]\" id=\"news-detail-aime-summary-panel-overview\" role=\"tabpanel\">\n        <div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-[12px] text-[14px] leading-[24px] text-text-primary @sm:text-[16px] @sm:leading-[26px]\">\n         <p>- Alphabet's 2026 capital spending ($205B) drives triple-digit cloud revenue growth (103% YoY) with 36% margins, contrasting market \"AI bubble\" narratives.</p>\n         <p>- <span class=\"inline\"><a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-AAPL/\">Apple</a><span class=\"relative flex w-full flex-wrap items-start gap-[8px] mx-[6px] inline-flex !w-auto align-baseline\"><span class=\"inline-flex\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-[4px] rounded-full border border-divider-level2 bg-transparent px-[12px] py-[7px] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] text-text-primary no-underline outline-none transition-colors hover:border-background-weak hover:bg-background-weak dark:bg-brand-primary/10 dark:hover:bg-brand-primary/15\"><a class=\"flex items-center text-inherit no-underline outline-none\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-AAPL/\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-[4px]\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums]\">AAPL</span><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums] min-w-[55px] text-text-tertiary\">--</span></span></a></span></span></span></span> (+26.8% YTD) dominates as \"safe\" haven at 36x forward P/E, while Alphabet trades at 15x trailing P/E despite $561B cloud backlog.</p>\n         <p>- Waymo's 500K+ weekly paid rides outpace Tesla's Cybercab plans, yet <span class=\"inline\"><a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-TSLA/\">Tesla</a><span class=\"relative flex w-full flex-wrap items-start gap-[8px] mx-[6px] inline-flex !w-auto align-baseline\"><span class=\"inline-flex\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-[4px] rounded-full border border-divider-level2 bg-transparent px-[12px] py-[7px] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] text-text-primary no-underline outline-none transition-colors hover:border-background-weak hover:bg-background-weak dark:bg-brand-primary/10 dark:hover:bg-brand-primary/15\"><a class=\"flex items-center text-inherit no-underline outline-none\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-TSLA/\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-[4px]\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums]\">TSLA</span><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums] min-w-[55px] text-text-tertiary\">--</span></span></a></span></span></span></span> trades at 200x forward P/E vs. Alphabet's discounted valuation.</p>\n         <p>- Market consensus misprices risk: Alphabet's $5.7T debt and capex must convert to cash flow - next quarterly operating cash flow will validate or refute bubble fears.</p>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n     </section>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"NewsDetailArticleContent-module__4HEp7a__content mb-[20px] w-full text-[18px] leading-[27px] text-text-primary\">\n     <article style=\"max-width:740px;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1.5rem;box-sizing:border-box\">\n      <div class=\"my-[24px] flex w-full items-center justify-center\">\n       <div class=\"w-full max-w-[600px]\">\n        <div class=\"flex h-[68px] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-[16px] bg-foreground-layer1\">\n         <span aria-label=\"Loading\" class=\"size-[28px] animate-spin rounded-full border-[2px] border-divider-level2 border-t-brand-primary\" role=\"status\"></span>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <p>The Magnificent Seven has become the Lonely One. Through the first ten months of 2026, <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/meet-only-magnificent-seven-stock-135000209.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">Apple rose about 27%</a> while every other member of the group trailed the S&amp;P 500 — <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/meet-only-magnificent-seven-stock-135000209.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">Alphabet down almost 11%, Tesla down 11%, Meta down 7%</a> — and a brand-new fund launched to track the group \"minus one,\" <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.etftrends.com/equity-etf-content-hub/global-x-etf-magnificent-seven-minus-tsla/\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">dropping Tesla from the basket by design</a>. Then came the crash everyone had been predicting. AI-linked stocks <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.hokanews.com/2026/11/ai-stocks-lose-132-trillion-in-market.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">erased a combined $13.2 trillion in market value from their 2026 highs</a>, and the Nasdaq fell into correction on <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/06/dan-ives-says-tech-rout-is-golden-buying-opportunity-.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">its worst day since the post-tariff rout of April 2025</a>. The lesson the market has settled on sounds simple and safe: AI was a debt-funded bubble, and the place to hide was <span class=\"inline\"><a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-AAPL/\">Apple</a><span class=\"relative flex w-full flex-wrap items-start gap-[8px] mx-[6px] inline-flex !w-auto align-baseline\"><span class=\"inline-flex\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-[4px] rounded-full border border-divider-level2 bg-transparent px-[12px] py-[7px] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] text-text-primary no-underline outline-none transition-colors hover:border-background-weak hover:bg-background-weak dark:bg-brand-primary/10 dark:hover:bg-brand-primary/15\"><a class=\"flex items-center text-inherit no-underline outline-none\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-AAPL/\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-[4px]\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums]\">AAPL</span><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums] min-w-[55px] text-text-tertiary\">--</span></span></a></span></span></span></span>, the one five-trillion-dollar company that isn't racing to build data centers. This is the argument that the trade has it exactly backward.</p>\n      <figure class=\"story-artifact chart\" data-artifact-id=\"chart-1\" style=\"margin:1rem 0;overflow-x:auto\">\n       <img alt=\"chart-1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"h-auto max-w-full rounded-[4px]\" style=\"color:transparent\" src=\"https://cdn.ainvest.com/news/visual/visual_components/chart-1-be756533df3b.png?format=webp\">\n       <div style=\"max-height:560px;max-width:100%;overflow:auto;-webkit-overflow-scrolling:touch\">\n        <div class=\"ArticleTable-module__OEcCVG__wrapper\">\n         <div class=\"ArticleTable-module__OEcCVG__tableFrame\">\n          <div class=\"ArticleTable-module__OEcCVG__scrollShell\">\n           <table class=\"ArticleTable-module__OEcCVG__table\" style=\"min-width:max(100%, 480px)\">\n            <colgroup>\n             <col style=\"min-width:160px;width:160px\">\n             <col style=\"min-width:160px;width:160px\">\n             <col style=\"min-width:160px;width:160px\">\n            </colgroup>\n            <thead>\n             <tr>\n              <th>Rank</th>\n              <th>Company</th>\n              <th>2026 YTD return (%)</th>\n             </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody>\n             <tr>\n              <td>1</td>\n              <td>Apple</td>\n              <td>+26.8</td>\n             </tr>\n             <tr>\n              <td>2</td>\n              <td>Nvidia</td>\n              <td>+9.7</td>\n             </tr>\n             <tr>\n              <td>3</td>\n              <td>Microsoft</td>\n              <td>+7.9</td>\n             </tr>\n             <tr>\n              <td>4</td>\n              <td>Amazon</td>\n              <td>+4.1</td>\n             </tr>\n             <tr>\n              <td>5</td>\n              <td>Meta Platforms</td>\n              <td>-6.8</td>\n             </tr>\n             <tr>\n              <td>6</td>\n              <td>Alphabet</td>\n              <td>-10.6</td>\n             </tr>\n             <tr>\n              <td>7</td>\n              <td>Tesla</td>\n              <td>-11.1</td>\n             </tr>\n            </tbody>\n           </table>\n          </div>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </figure>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:1.5em 0 .5em\">Everyone is watching the capex line. Nobody counts what it buys.</h2>\n      <p>Every doomsday headline pins the bubble on the same number: capital spending. Alphabet has told investors it <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.insiderfinance.io/news/alphabet-q3-2026-earnings-cloud-growth-capex-rise\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">will spend up to $205 billion on capex in 2026, mostly on AI, and says the total will climb</a> \"significantly\" in 2027. Across the group, the borrowing to fund the buildout has swelled — SBI Research puts the seven companies' <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/tech/artificial-intelligence/ai-debt-surge-pushes-magnificent-seven-borrowing-to-usd-578-billion-up-45-sbi-research/articleshow/135443806.cms\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">combined debt at roughly $578 billion by mid-2026, up 45% in a year</a>. Count the dollars being shoveled into the ground and the story writes itself: this is a bubble.</p>\n      <p>But a capex number is not a verdict. Capital spending is an investment, and its value lives entirely in what it produces. The denominator that decides whether $205 billion is reckless or rational is not the size of the check — it is how much revenue that check actually converts into. The consensus forecast below shows why the spending dominates the conversation: across Alphabet, Amazon, Microsoft, <span class=\"inline\"><a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-META/\">Meta</a><span class=\"relative flex w-full flex-wrap items-start gap-[8px] mx-[6px] inline-flex !w-auto align-baseline\"><span class=\"inline-flex\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-[4px] rounded-full border border-divider-level2 bg-transparent px-[12px] py-[7px] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] text-text-primary no-underline outline-none transition-colors hover:border-background-weak hover:bg-background-weak dark:bg-brand-primary/10 dark:hover:bg-brand-primary/15\"><a class=\"flex items-center text-inherit no-underline outline-none\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-META/\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-[4px]\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums]\">META</span><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums] min-w-[55px] text-text-tertiary\">--</span></span></a></span></span></span></span> and Oracle, analysts see capex climbing through 2027, a trajectory the market read as proof of excess.</p>\n      <section aria-label=\"Quick backtesting tool\" class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__container\">\n       <h2 class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__title\">Quick Backtesting Tool</h2>\n       <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__toolContent\">\n        <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldGroup NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldSymbol\">\n         <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldContainer\">\n          <span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__label\">Symbol</span><button class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__inputContainer\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__symbolInfo\"><span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__valueText\">GOOG</span></span></button>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldGroup NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldStrategy\">\n         <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldContainer\">\n          <span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__label\">Strategy</span>\n          <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__inputContainer NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__dropdownInputContainer\">\n           <div>\n            <button type=\"button\" id=\"radix-_R_2kdpkj9lav5ubslmlb_\" aria-haspopup=\"menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-state=\"closed\" data-slot=\"dropdown-menu-trigger\" class=\"flex w-full\"> \n             <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__inputButton\">\n              <span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__valueText NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__placeholderText\">Select</span>\n             </div> \n            </button>\n           </div>\n          </div>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldGroup NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldTimeRange\">\n         <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__fieldContainer\">\n          <span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__label\">Backtest Range</span>\n          <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__inputContainer NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__dropdownInputContainer\">\n           <div>\n            <button type=\"button\" id=\"radix-_R_2sdpkj9lav5ubslmlb_\" aria-haspopup=\"menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-state=\"closed\" data-slot=\"dropdown-menu-trigger\" class=\"flex w-full\"> \n             <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__inputButton\">\n              <span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__valueText\">Past 5 years</span>\n             </div> \n            </button>\n           </div>\n          </div>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__footer\">\n        <button class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__runButton\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__runButtonText\">Run backtest</span></button><button class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__moreButton\" type=\"button\"><span class=\"NewsDetailBacktest-module__wzanNG__moreButtonText\">More Backtesting Ideas</span></button>\n       </div>\n      </section>\n      <!-- -->\n      <figure data-source-image-id=\"img_9f48e94bfbbdd4ab\">\n       <img alt=\"This table provides a qualitative summary of capital expenditures (CapEx) for five major hyperscale companies: Amazon (AMZN), Alphabet (GOOG), Meta (META), Microsoft (MSFT), and Oracle (ORCL). It details management commentary for the current and next quarters, as well as full-year 2026 guidance. The table includes consensus estimates for CapEx for calendar years 2025, 2026, and 2027. Specific drivers mentioned include AI datacenter buildouts, GPU infrastructure, and Azure demand. A total hyperscale CapEx row aggregates the consensus figures across the three years. Microsoft figures are noted to include finance leases, while Meta figures exclude them.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"h-auto max-w-full rounded-[4px]\" style=\"color:transparent\" src=\"https://cdn.ainvest.com/news/visual/visual_components/img_9f48e94bfbbdd4ab-505e77b826ce.png?format=webp\">\n       <figcaption style=\"font-size:0.875em;line-height:1.5;color:#666;margin-top:0.5em\">\n        <em>Hyperscale Capital Expenditures Commentary and Consensus Estimates — <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://cdn.ainvest.com/news/visual/visual_components/img_9f48e94bfbbdd4ab-0a335f26a718.png\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">TD Cowen</a> — 2026-08-17</em>\n       </figcaption>\n      </figure>\n      <div class=\"my-[24px] flex w-full items-center justify-center\">\n       <div class=\"w-full max-w-[600px]\">\n        <div class=\"flex h-[68px] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-[16px] bg-foreground-layer1\">\n         <span aria-label=\"Loading\" class=\"size-[28px] animate-spin rounded-full border-[2px] border-divider-level2 border-t-brand-primary\" role=\"status\"></span>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:1.5em 0 .5em\">The part of the spend that already doubled</h2>\n      <p>Here is the conversion the panic is ignoring. Alphabet reported third-quarter Google Cloud revenue <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.insiderfinance.io/news/alphabet-q3-2026-earnings-cloud-growth-capex-rise\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">up 103% year over year to $30.7 billion, with operating income reaching $11.1 billion on a 36% operating margin, up from 24% a year earlier</a>. That is not a distant promise; it is current, high-margin, profitable revenue growing at triple digits, and the division holds <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/11/04/alphabets-free-cash-flow-is-declining-faster-than/\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">about $561 billion of contracted backlog, more than half of which the company expects to turn into revenue over the next two years</a>.</p>\n      <div class=\"my-[24px] flex w-full items-center justify-center\">\n       <div class=\"w-full max-w-[600px]\">\n        <div class=\"flex h-[68px] w-full items-center justify-center rounded-[16px] bg-foreground-layer1\">\n         <span aria-label=\"Loading\" class=\"size-[28px] animate-spin rounded-full border-[2px] border-divider-level2 border-t-brand-primary\" role=\"status\"></span>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <p>This is the mechanism the bubble story does not fit. The money going into data centers is already showing up on Alphabet's income statement as fast-growing, high-margin, booked cloud revenue — plus <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.insiderfinance.io/news/alphabet-q3-2026-earnings-cloud-growth-capex-rise\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">TPU systems, whose sales the company says will keep scaling into next year</a>. When capex becomes revenue this quickly, the charge that it is a black hole deserves re-examination rather than repetition.</p>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:1.5em 0 .5em\">Cheap because it's hated. The \"safe\" trade is the crowded one.</h2>\n      <p>Strip away the panic and the price does the contrarian work. Alphabet has <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.hokanews.com/2026/11/ai-stocks-lose-132-trillion-in-market.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">lost roughly a third of its value from the 2026 high</a>, and the Motley Fool notes it <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/11/04/alphabets-free-cash-flow-is-declining-faster-than/\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">now trades around 15 times trailing earnings, below the roughly 24 times the average tech company carries</a>. The market has decided, in other words, that this is the broken artificial-intelligence name.</p>\n      <p><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"h-auto max-w-full rounded-[4px]\" style=\"color:transparent\" src=\"https://cdn.ainvest.com/aigc/hxcmp/images/compress-qwen_generated_1794163810791.jpg.png?format=webp\"></p>\n      <p>Now look at the escape hatch everyone ran to. Apple sits <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nasdaq-stock-market-correction-heres-154101537.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">about 2% below its high at roughly 36 times forward earnings</a>, the most expensive and most crowded \"safe\" stock in the group. There is the inversion in its purest form: the market is paying a premium for the one company not investing in the next decade's technology, and selling at a discount the one that is — yet still <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.insiderfinance.io/news/alphabet-q3-2026-earnings-cloud-growth-capex-rise\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">grows search advertising 12% a year</a>, runs <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nasdaq-stock-market-correction-heres-154101537.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">a Gemini assistant reaching a billion users</a>, and <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nasdaq-stock-market-correction-heres-154101537.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">grew total operating income 30% to $40.6 billion</a> even while ramping its AI spending.</p>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:1.5em 0 .5em\">The self-driving story already belongs to Alphabet, not Tesla</h2>\n      <!-- -->\n      <p>None of this is the familiar <span class=\"inline\"><a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-TSLA/\">Tesla</a><span class=\"relative flex w-full flex-wrap items-start gap-[8px] mx-[6px] inline-flex !w-auto align-baseline\"><span class=\"inline-flex\"><span class=\"inline-flex items-center gap-[4px] rounded-full border border-divider-level2 bg-transparent px-[12px] py-[7px] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] text-text-primary no-underline outline-none transition-colors hover:border-background-weak hover:bg-background-weak dark:bg-brand-primary/10 dark:hover:bg-brand-primary/15\"><a class=\"flex items-center text-inherit no-underline outline-none\" href=\"https://www.ainvest.com/stocks/NASDAQ-TSLA/\"><span class=\"flex items-center gap-[4px]\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums]\">TSLA</span><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center text-center font-[&quot;Plus_Jakarta_Sans&quot;] text-[14px] font-medium leading-[12px] [font-variant-numeric:lining-nums_tabular-nums] min-w-[55px] text-text-tertiary\">--</span></span></a></span></span></span></span> storyline, and that is the point. The market still <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nasdaq-stock-market-correction-heres-154101537.html\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">pays Tesla roughly 200 times forward earnings</a> for an autonomous future that begins later this decade. But the autonomous business operating at scale today — <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.dailytraderinsights.com/2026/09/03/waymo-now-runs-500000-rides-a-week-a-48-billion-industry-is-taking-shape/\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">more than 500,000 paid rides a week across 14 U.S. markets, heading toward a million weekly by year-end</a> — is Alphabet's Waymo. Tesla, meanwhile, <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.channelnewsasia.com/business/tesla-expand-cybertruck-production-in-bid-fill-orders-dismantling-line-next-year-6533391\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">plans to dismantle its Cybertruck line next year to make room for the Cybercab</a>, a vehicle not yet shipping in meaningful volume. The robotaxi promise is already priced into Tesla at a triple-digit multiple; the operating version of it sits buried inside Alphabet's \"Other Bets,\" the line investors most readily dismiss as an R&amp;D cost center.</p>\n      <h2 style=\"margin:1.5em 0 .5em\">The honest risk, and the one line that settles it</h2>\n      <p>None of this is free, and the contrarian call can lose. Alphabet's free cash flow is genuinely falling as capex climbs — <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/11/04/alphabets-free-cash-flow-is-declining-faster-than/\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">$5.2 billion of this year's decline was a one-time European Commission fine</a>, but the guide to <a class=\"text-brand-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.insiderfinance.io/news/alphabet-q3-2026-earnings-cloud-growth-capex-rise\" rel=\"noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"\">spend \"significantly more\" in 2027</a> is a real, dated risk. Ainvest data show Amazon is the cautionary template: its capex now exceeds its own operating cash flow. If Alphabet keeps converting spend into revenue the way the last quarter did, the priced-in crash is a gift; if its cash flow starts to stall while the spending climbs, Google becomes an Amazon-style case and the bubble reading wins.</p>\n      <p>The single number that separates the two is Alphabet's operating cash flow on its next quarterly report. As long as that figure keeps growing even as the company spends toward $205 billion and beyond, the buildout is paying for itself out of its own operations, and you would be buying the cheapest large AI name at the moment of maximum fear. If it turns down while the capex turns up, the crowd was right about Google's spending — and you see it in one dated print, not in hindsight. The panic has already priced one of those outcomes. The cash-flow line tells you which one is true.</p>\n     </article>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "尽管 Alphabet 投入 $205B 资本开支、云业务积压订单达 $561B，且 Q3 云收入同比增长 103% 至 $30.7B，但其估值仅为 15x 市盈率；在市场因债务融资支出而陷入恐慌之际，它因此成为大型 AI 公司中估值最低的一家。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "尽管 Alphabet 投入 $205B 资本开支、云业务积压订单达 $561B，且 Q3 云收入同比增长 103% 至 $30.7B，但其估值仅为 15x 市盈率；在市场因债务融资支出而陷入恐慌之际，它因此成为大型 AI 公司中估值最低的一家。",
  "summary": "市场抹去 AI 概念股 $13.2T 市值后，将 Alphabet 定价为「陷入困境」的 AI 股票，其滚动市盈率仅为 15x。然而，2026 年 Q3，Google Cloud 创造了 $30.7B 营收（同比增长 103%），营业利润率达 36%，合同积压订单达 $561B。尽管 2026 年资本开支达 $205B（2027 年还将大幅增加），助长了「泡沫」论调，但支出迅速转化为高利润率收入，正在挑战这种看法。Apple 的预期市盈率为 36x，尽管没有投资下一代技术，却被视为「安全」避风港；Tesla 则凭借尚未得到验证的 Cybercab，拥有 200x 的预期市盈率。Waymo 已在美国 14 个市场每周提供超过 500K 次付费乘车服务，但其自动驾驶业务被归入投资者视为研发项目的「其他业务」之中。关键风险在于：随着资本开支持续攀升，Alphabet 的自由现金流正在下降。下一季度的经营现金流报告将成为关键验证点，决定这些支出能否收回成本。",
  "mainPoints": [
